{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Model pricing per million tokens (USD). Keys use dashes (no dots) for consistent normalization.",
    "sources": {
      "Anthropic": "platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing",
      "OpenAI": "developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing",
      "Google": "ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing",
      "xAI": "docs.x.ai/developers/models",
      "DeepSeek": "api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing",
      "Z.ai": "docs.z.ai/guides/overview/pricing",
      "Zen": "opencode.ai/docs/zen/"
    },
    "lastVerified": "2026-11",
    "notes": {
      "keys": "All keys use dashes instead of dots (e.g. gpt-5-4 not gpt-5.4) so normalizeModelName dots→dashes works",
      "cacheRead": "cache hit price. Usually 0.1x input, but not always: Anthropic Fable/Mythos 5.1 and 5.2 are 0.025x, Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5 are 0.05x; OpenAI GPT-6.1 Sol/Terra are 0.05x. Models with no cached discount (gpt-*-pro, o3-pro, gpt-3.5-turbo) set cacheRead = input, because the Codex adapter subtracts cached tokens from input.",
      "cacheWrite": "cache write price. Anthropic: 5-minute write, 1.25x input on every model (1h write is 2x). OpenAI: GPT-5.6 and later bill the 30-minute write at 1.25x input. Providers with no separate write charge (OpenAI GPT-5.5 and earlier, Google, xAI, DeepSeek) bill written tokens as normal input, so cacheWrite = input (a few legacy entries still carry 0).",
      "gemini-4-carbon": "ACTION REQUIRED 2026-12-01: gemini-4-carbon and gemini-4-argon are $2/$10 (cr 0.10) only through 2026-11-30; from 2026-12-01 they are $4/$20 (cr 0.20, cw 4) per the official page.",
      "gemini-3-8-flash": "ACTION REQUIRED 2027-01-01: gemini-3-8-flash and gemini-3-6-flash (and gemini-3-7-flash / gemini-flash-latest, which route to them) are $0.75/$3.75 (cr 0.075) through 2026-12-31, then $1.50/$7.50 (cr 0.15, cw 1.5). Gemini -latest alias targets are not published; values follow models.dev.",
      "claude-sonnet-5": "Resolved: Anthropic made the $2/$10 introductory price permanent (official pricing footnote). The $3/$15 increase scheduled for 2026-09-01 did not happen.",
      "claude-haiku-5-5": "Tiered by prompt length. Entry holds the <=100K tier ($0.10/$0.50, cr 0.01, cw 0.125). A request whose prompt (incl. cache reads/writes) exceeds 100K pays $0.50/$2.50, cr 0.05, cw 0.625 on all its tokens; pricing.json cannot express this, so long-prompt Haiku 5.5 requests are under-priced 5x.",
      "gpt-5-6-sol": "ACTION REQUIRED 2026-12-01: $4/$20 (cr 0.4, cw 5) is promotional pricing valid until 2026-11-30 (official footnote). OpenAI describes it as a 20% input / 33% output cut, implying about $5/$30 after; re-check the official page and update gpt-5-6-sol, gpt-5-6 and gpt-daybreak-blue-latest (aliases of Sol).",
      "longContext": "Entries hold the base tier only. OpenAI GPT-6/5.6/5.5/5.4 bill the whole request at 2x input/cached/write and 1.5x output above 272K input tokens. xAI bills all tokens at roughly 2x once the prompt reaches 200K. Google Gemini Pro models have a higher >200K tier. Anthropic 4.6+ (except Haiku 5.5) has no long-context tier.",
      "deepseek": "Since 2026-08-16 DeepSeek prices by time of day. Entries hold OFF-PEAK rates; peak (01:00-04:00 and 06:00-10:00 UTC, Mon-Fri) is 2x. deepseek-chat/deepseek-reasoner were retired 2026-07-24 and kept for historical usage. deepseek-v4-pro was $0.435/$0.87 before 2026-08-16; flat pricing re-prices older sessions at today's rate.",
      "minimax": "minimax-m3 is $0.30/$1.20 (cr 0.06) for <=512K input after a permanent 50% discount; >512K input is $0.60/$2.40 (cr 0.12) for the whole request. M2.x models (M2.7, M2.5, M2.1, M2 and highspeed variants) are retired / retiring 2026-11-18 and kept for historical usage; their rows come from the archived official page.",
      "xai": "grok-4-0709, grok-4-1-fast*, grok-3 and grok-code-fast-1 were retired 2026-05-15 and redirect to grok-4.3 / grok-build-0.1 (billed at grok-4.3 rates). Their legacy entries are kept at historical prices for older sessions.",
      "fastMode": "Fast mode (speed:'fast') uses the same model string, so it prices at standard rates here. Anthropic fast: Opus 5.5 $8/$40, Fable/Mythos 5.2 $16/$80, Opus 5 and 4.8 $10/$50 (Opus 4.8 fast mode removed 2026-11-30). OpenAI Fast mode (formerly Priority): 2x for GPT-6/5.6, 2.5x for GPT-5.5."
    }
  },
